1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:03,490
Certifications brings together the types
your department tracks and

2
00:00:03,490 --> 00:00:05,699
the records held by people or units.

3
00:00:06,090 --> 00:00:09,600
In this fictional Chicago Fire department,
the dashboard starts

4
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,800
with one record pending verification.

5
00:00:12,329 --> 00:00:17,159
Boden can inspect his own pending record,
but this page offers no Verify button.

6
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:20,399
Record holders cannot verify their own
records.

7
00:00:20,829 --> 00:00:25,120
We will create a clearly marked software
exercise for another member, then use

8
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:27,180
the normal administrative review path.

9
00:00:27,659 --> 00:00:31,940
Use the viewing, management, and setup
permissions your department has assigned.

10
00:00:32,139 --> 00:00:33,830
Choose Certification types.

11
00:00:34,230 --> 00:00:38,849
The table separates each stable code,
category, scope, validity,

12
00:00:39,099 --> 00:00:41,149
record count, and requirement count.

13
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:44,330
Template gallery opens a separate
selection window.

14
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:49,000
Enter SAR in its filter to inspect
relevant starter entries.

15
00:00:49,319 --> 00:00:53,559
Their displayed names, authorities, and
validity periods are catalog starting

16
00:00:53,559 --> 00:00:55,610
points that your department must review.

17
00:00:56,010 --> 00:01:00,030
Keep every checkbox clear and use Cancel;
nothing is added.

18
00:01:00,409 --> 00:01:04,109
We will create our own fictional Person
type so the software exercise

19
00:01:04,109 --> 00:01:06,170
is distinct from the existing types.

20
00:01:06,370 --> 00:01:07,570
Choose New type.

21
00:01:08,089 --> 00:01:11,490
Enter Training Only, Record Review,
followed by the

22
00:01:11,490 --> 00:01:13,180
exercise date, as the Type.

23
00:01:13,519 --> 00:01:18,960
Give it the explicit code
TRN-REVIEW-20261028.

24
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:23,750
A stable, recognizable code helps
distinguish this type

25
00:01:23,779 --> 00:01:25,750
later in tables and integrations.

26
00:01:26,110 --> 00:01:29,709
Keep Category as Other and Applies to as
Person.

27
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:34,729
Enter Academy Software Exercise, marked
fictional, as the Issuing authority.

28
00:01:35,039 --> 00:01:39,599
The Description explicitly identifies a
software verification exercise and

29
00:01:39,599 --> 00:01:43,290
says that it is not a professional
qualification or authorization.

30
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:47,729
Set Default validity to twelve months and
leave Never expires clear.

31
00:01:48,159 --> 00:01:50,300
Credit hours per renewal stays blank.

32
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:54,839
Check Requires supervisor verification and
keep Active checked.

33
00:01:55,259 --> 00:01:58,860
The help explains that new records remain
pending until someone with

34
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:00,550
management rights signs them off.

35
00:02:00,909 --> 00:02:03,860
Use Save, then read the returned catalog
row.

36
00:02:04,329 --> 00:02:09,019
Our code is present, its scope is Person,
and its validity is twelve months.

37
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:12,649
Both Records and Requirements are zero:
creating this type

38
00:02:12,649 --> 00:02:16,259
has not created a member record or
attached a role requirement.

39
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:19,229
On the dashboard, choose Add
Certification.

40
00:02:19,689 --> 00:02:22,919
This administrative form has an explicit
Member selector.

41
00:02:23,309 --> 00:02:26,809
Choose Matthew Casey, then select the new
training type.

42
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:30,389
Check the selected member and type
together before entering

43
00:02:30,389 --> 00:02:31,780
identifying information.

44
00:02:32,189 --> 00:02:37,100
Notice that Issued on and Expires on are
still blank after selecting the type.

45
00:02:37,490 --> 00:02:41,109
The type’s twelve-month setting has not
filled these fields on this form.

46
00:02:41,479 --> 00:02:45,129
We will enter the intended exercise dates
explicitly rather than

47
00:02:45,129 --> 00:02:46,910
assume that a date was calculated.

48
00:02:47,149 --> 00:02:51,310
Use Training Only, Software Record Review
as the Name and the

49
00:02:51,310 --> 00:02:54,259
DEMO-CASEY-REVIEW number shown here.

50
00:02:54,659 --> 00:02:59,269
Valid Area says Academy training
department only, and Issued by

51
00:02:59,359 --> 00:03:01,420
repeats our fictional software issuer.

52
00:03:01,830 --> 00:03:04,919
Enter October twenty-eighth, twenty
twenty-six as the issue

53
00:03:04,919 --> 00:03:08,890
date and October twenty-eighth, twenty
twenty-seven as the expiry.

54
00:03:09,279 --> 00:03:11,499
File is optional and remains empty.

55
00:03:11,849 --> 00:03:12,820
Save once.

56
00:03:13,179 --> 00:03:17,509
The returned dashboard reports Saved and
now has two pending records.

57
00:03:17,829 --> 00:03:21,870
Saving the record did not automatically
complete its required verification.

58
00:03:22,119 --> 00:03:23,790
Here is Casey’s saved record.

59
00:03:24,230 --> 00:03:28,830
Read its member, type, number, and expiry
before using Verify.

60
00:03:29,270 --> 00:03:31,409
This button submits the review directly.

61
00:03:31,830 --> 00:03:35,330
The returned record is Active and shows
Verified by Wallace

62
00:03:35,330 --> 00:03:36,970
Boden with the displayed date.

63
00:03:37,359 --> 00:03:41,069
Open the record again and check that the
same status and reviewer remain.

64
00:03:41,430 --> 00:03:43,620
This confirms the stored software review.

65
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,010
It does not establish that a real
qualification was earned.

66
00:03:47,399 --> 00:03:50,760
We leave renewal, credits, suspension, and
revocation

67
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:52,889
unchanged throughout this exercise.

68
00:03:53,069 --> 00:03:56,099
Use Matthew Casey’s member link to open
his holdings.

69
00:03:56,540 --> 00:04:02,140
The table lists each record separately
with its name, type, expiry, and status.

70
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:06,159
The existing Firefighter qualification
remains, and the new training

71
00:04:06,159 --> 00:04:10,119
review appears on another row with its own
date and Active status.

72
00:04:10,490 --> 00:04:15,060
Compare the exact record name and type
before opening or editing anything.

73
00:04:15,449 --> 00:04:19,570
This person view helps you distinguish a
newly added exercise record from an

74
00:04:19,609 --> 00:04:21,880
older record that should remain untouched.

75
00:04:22,050 --> 00:04:24,089
Return through Certification types.

76
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:28,179
Our row now has one Record and still has
zero Requirements.

77
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:31,750
Use that row’s Edit control to inspect the
saved type.

78
00:04:32,090 --> 00:04:35,949
Applies to is disabled at Person because a
record now references it.

79
00:04:36,340 --> 00:04:39,819
Code remains editable here; code locking
applies when role

80
00:04:39,819 --> 00:04:41,450
requirements reference the type.

81
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:45,149
The lower options still show twelve
months, verification

82
00:04:45,149 --> 00:04:47,090
required, and Active checked.

83
00:04:47,420 --> 00:04:48,940
This is a readback only.

84
00:04:49,190 --> 00:04:53,680
We do not change the code, add a role
requirement, or save another type update.

85
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:57,629
Settings separates role enforcement from
expiry notifications.

86
00:04:57,999 --> 00:05:02,390
The saved mode is Off, with thirty days of
grace and pending records not

87
00:05:02,390 --> 00:05:04,499
treated as valid for role requirements.

88
00:05:04,909 --> 00:05:09,419
Warn only permits role changes with
warnings; Enforce can block

89
00:05:09,449 --> 00:05:12,899
unqualified role additions and remove
members after grace.

90
00:05:13,350 --> 00:05:17,530
We inspect these choices, restore Off, and
leave Save untouched.

91
00:05:17,940 --> 00:05:21,630
Off does not disable expiry processing or
notifications.

92
00:05:22,059 --> 00:05:26,400
The holder and administrator-digest
options remain checked, with lead days of

93
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:29,970
sixty, thirty, fourteen, seven, and one.

94
00:05:30,409 --> 00:05:32,779
These settings do not prove message
delivery.

95
00:05:33,010 --> 00:05:36,229
On the dashboard, Group is filtered to
Truck 81.

96
00:05:36,610 --> 00:05:40,989
Five member rows appear, including Casey’s
new expiry under the training code.

97
00:05:41,319 --> 00:05:44,350
The Pending verification card still
describes the department,

98
00:05:44,649 --> 00:05:46,260
not just these filtered rows.

99
00:05:46,649 --> 00:05:51,470
Export CSV is available for the current
filters; no file is downloaded here.

100
00:05:51,890 --> 00:05:54,939
Choose Compliance report to open the HTML
report.

101
00:05:55,359 --> 00:06:00,000
In Casey’s row, the training column shows
the same expiry and Active status.

102
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:04,640
Read that actual row rather than infer a
status from a color or a total.

103
00:06:04,799 --> 00:06:08,059
Chicago Fire can use this pattern to
organize a clearly

104
00:06:08,059 --> 00:06:09,749
identified exercise record.

105
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:13,400
Community care and mental health teams can
track operational

106
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:15,260
training without patient detail.

107
00:06:15,610 --> 00:06:19,329
Search and rescue can distinguish person
records from equipment records;

108
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:24,259
security teams can organize reviewed staff
records; wildland teams can keep

109
00:06:24,259 --> 00:06:28,769
seasonal training references current; and
industrial response teams can separate

110
00:06:28,769 --> 00:06:30,920
staff records from unit inspections.

111
00:06:31,299 --> 00:06:36,369
In every setting, define the type, enter
deliberate dates, use an authorized

112
00:06:36,369 --> 00:06:38,989
reviewer, and verify saved status.

113
00:06:39,340 --> 00:06:42,860
A software label alone does not authorize
real duties.

